keep-ram-clean for Debian
=========================

Configuration
-------------
The system-wide daemon reads /etc/keep-ram-clean/config.toml.
Edit trigger thresholds or schedules using:

  sudo keep-ram-clean config show
  sudo keep-ram-clean config set ram-percent 75

Systemd Service
---------------
The system service is installed to /usr/lib/systemd/system/keep-ram-clean.service
and is disabled by default until enabled by the administrator:

  sudo systemctl enable --now keep-ram-clean.service

A non-root user service is also provided at
/usr/lib/systemd/user/keep-ram-clean.service:

  systemctl --user enable --now keep-ram-clean.service
